# Constitution §2.1: source is LF-only. `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree
# regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf setting, which otherwise rewrites
# checkouts to CRLF on Windows and makes `gofmt -s -l .` (and the gofmt formatter
# in golangci-lint) report every file as unformatted.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content; the explicit binary overrides below
# are belt-and-braces for the asset types this repo actually tracks.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
